# Path ownership — OWN WHAT GOVERNS THE AGENT, NOT WHAT THE AGENT OPERATES ON (the homelab /
# agent-runtime shape). Narrowed 2026-10-13 (operator: homelab's rule work made the codeowner a
# non-blocker there; the platform repos were the ones still parking PRs — openrouter-operator#90
# sat REVIEW_REQUIRED with the reviewer's APPROVED at head and CI green on the 3.15 interpreter).
# Before this the whole repo was owned (2026-08-11, the reviewer-enable retrace: this repo builds
# the fleet's egress/credential/budget chokepoint, so a bot approval alone must never merge).
# The ruling that replaced it is homelab ADR-128/FU-233 (promoted after the trial week) extended
# to the platform repos (homelab ADR-154): src/, tests/, chart/ and the Dockerfile merge on CI +
# the reviewer bot — the rubric's read is the gate there, and the catches census
# (homelab docs/spikes/codeowner-catches.md: 4 src/ catches in 10 human reads, 2 outage-class)
# is the known cost the operator accepted. Still enforced only together with
# require_code_owner_review=true (homelab tofu/github/variables.tf) — without that ruleset flag
# this file is decorative. Revert = `git revert` of the narrowing commit.
#
# GitHub semantics: LAST matching pattern wins, and a pattern with NO owner REMOVES ownership.
# scripts/deps-pin-guard.sh reads this file at the merge-base to classify a mixed PR — only
# `*`, `/dir/` and `/path` shapes; anything fancier fails that guard closed.

# ── The repo's own checks. scripts/ holds ci.sh, deps-pin-guard.sh + deps_pin_shape.py (the
# dep lane's replacement owner), package-chart.sh and deploy-pin.sh (the publish path). A worker
# able to edit them is judged by the check it edited — homelab un-owned its scripts/ under ADR-142
# only with the gate-change lens + gate-drift report in place, and this repo carries neither
# (the lens selects on `scripts/gate-drift.sh` at the default branch). Owned until that port.
/scripts/           @RasmusSoot

# ── The build+publish workflows (deploy.yaml pushes the image and opens the deploy-pin PR into
# homelab), renovate-approve, ci. Owned; the action-pin lane is carved out below.
/.github/           @RasmusSoot

# ── Renovate's action-pin lane (homelab ADR-100 addendum / ADR-141, S9 #1990). Ownership is
# REPLACED, not dropped: `pin-only-lint` (homelab scripts/pin-only-lint.sh, run inside the
# required `ci` check) allows only verified action pin bumps (`uses: owner/repo@sha # tag`, the
# SHA resolved upstream to the tag's commit, pairs only, first-party refs frozen) through a PR;
# a real workflow edit takes the operator path straight to master, where the check does not run.
# Post-merge failures of push-only workflows roll back via the FU-1990 chain (drill passed on
# agent-coordinator, 2026-09-27). One-line revert: restore the owner below.
/.github/workflows/

# ── The recipes are the agent's own instructions — an agent able to edit them is not gated at
# all (the reviewer reads its rubric off the PR branch and refused to gate a change to its own
# rules, homelab PR#386).
/.agents/           @RasmusSoot

# ── The ownership file owns itself (the first thing an agent could otherwise propose is its own
# ungating).
/CODEOWNERS         @RasmusSoot

# ── Deliberately UNOWNED — CI + the reviewer bot are the gate:
#   src/, tests/, chart/, Dockerfile, README.md, CLAUDE.md, .pre-commit-config.yaml
# The dep files are un-owned too, with a REPLACEMENT owner: scripts/deps-pin-guard.sh in the
# required `ci` check admits only version/hash lines of EXISTING packages (devbox.json/lock since
# 2026-08-11; pyproject.toml/uv.lock since 2026-09-27 — scripts/deps_pin_shape.py is the
# contract: a new or removed package, requires-python or a tool-table edit is refused, and with
# nothing left to own the refusal parks on the operator's admin merge, as #90 did). Since
# 2026-10-13 that shape test also runs when the PR touches other un-owned paths (a worker's
# adaptation of a Renovate bump: lock refresh + Dockerfile); only an OWNED path in the PR puts the
# whole read on the code owner instead.
